// Recorder for node-files-chown.controls.json. Each case names an fs function and its arguments; the test runs the
// same cases, unchanged, against the emulated functions. Run with Node 24.18.1 once as an ordinary user and once as root:
//   docker run --rm --user 1000:1000 --tmpfs /work:mode=1777 -v "$PWD":/w:ro node:24.18.1-alpine node /w/record.cjs > user.json
//   docker run --rm --tmpfs /work:mode=1777 -v "$PWD":/w:ro node:24.18.1-alpine node /w/record.cjs answers > root.json
// `answers` keeps the cases Linux answers and leaves out the argument checks, which do not depend on the caller.
// The controls file is { node, recorder: <this file>, user: <user.json>, root: <root.json> }.
// "$fd" in the arguments is a descriptor of /work/file, "$bad" one that is not open, and { $: kind } a value JSON
// cannot hold. Every case starts from a fresh /work/file and /work/link -> file, both owned by the caller.
const fs = require("fs");
